Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Aug 13 21:33:44 2026 -0500

    fix(lang): SOL-R4-01 — refuse vertex mutation outside the scanner's provable domain
    
    Arbiter ruling: end the lexical-evasion arms race with conservative
    refusal. The multiplicity and comment guards are quote-aware over plain
    KDL strings only; raw strings (#"…"# / ##"…"##) and multi-line strings
    are outside that provable domain, so add/edit/remove_vertex_kind now
    refuse with a typed, actionable ValueError when the vertex text contains
    those delimiters. No KDL lexer built — the .vertex corpus has zero raw
    strings (15 files; the 10 repo raw-string hits are all .loop source
    lines, a different file type outside the mutation domain). Parser oracle
    stays as the in-domain backstop.
    
