commit 0663c705cd3d4cdf72e77412361326bd4954da70
Author:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Thu Aug 13 21:37:15 2026 -0500
Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Aug 13 21:37:15 2026 -0500

    fix(engine): SOL-R4-03 — JSONL log serializes the COMMITTED read-back row
    
    The canonical log is a pure derivation of the committed index, so the
    log line now serializes the COMPLETE row read back post-INSERT (AFTER
    triggers fired), pre-commit, pre-any-log-byte — never the caller-
    assembled row. A trigger-rewritten row can no longer put one truth in
    the index and another in the log (audit_agreement stays green). An
    absent read-back row refuses via CommittedRowMissing (composes with
    SOL-R4-02), log untouched. The codec pre-flight on the assembled row is
    retained ahead of the INSERT so sqlite column affinity cannot coerce a
    codec-invalid row into something committable.
    
    Regression: sol's signature-nulling-trigger repro — log now derive-
    matches the index and audit_agreement passes; untriggered append pinned.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C9MfGCNdAoSqKQ34mKevuF

