commit 010a97b9be3b71ed49328d1cc838037fdcc98670
Author:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Thu Aug 13 21:45:37 2026 -0500
Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Aug 13 21:45:37 2026 -0500

    fix(engine): ceremony read-back refuses on ANY committed-row divergence
    
    Arbiter ruling on the R4 needs-arbiter residue: signatures cover the
    final persisted payload (ratified encoding contract), so a trigger-
    rewritten non-signature field leaves a signature that no longer
    verifies against its row — serializing either the assembled or the
    mutated row would persist a verification lie. absorb_genesis and
    absorb_edit now compare the COMPLETE committed row (all persisted
    columns, via _committed_full_row hoisted from JsonlStore into
    SqliteStore — one spelling, jsonl duplicate dissolved) against the
    assembled row, and refuse with UnsignableGenesis/UnsignableEdit +
    rollback before any log byte on any mismatch. Absent rows keep the
    CommittedRowMissing refusal (SOL-R4-02).
    
    Regression (red-first): origin-rewriting AFTER INSERT trigger against
    both genesis and edit ceremonies — typed refusal, nothing committed.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C9MfGCNdAoSqKQ34mKevuF

