+Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
+CommitDate: Thu Aug 13 21:04:14 2026 -0500
+
+    fix(lang): SOL-R3-01 — parser-oracle blind spots: duplicate-kind precondition, requested-definition assert, edit trailing-comment honesty
+    
+    (a) duplicate loop-kind nodes in the input refuse typed before mutation —
+    the parser collapses them last-wins, so the oracle cannot see them; a raw-
+    text multiplicity check at the splitter layer is a pre-condition on the
+    input, not a safety detector. (b) after add/edit the target kind's parsed
+    definition must EQUAL the requested LoopDef (belt-and-braces under (a)).
+    (c) edit preserves the suffix after the block's final close; a comment
+    inside the replaced span refuses with an actionable message instead of
+    silently dropping.
+    
+    Arbiter ruling on SOL-R3-01 (blocker). Regression: sol's three repros.
+    
+    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
+    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C9MfGCNdAoSqKQ34mKevuF
+
